  "question": "求极限 $\\lim_{n\\to \\infty}\\frac{1}{n}\\sqrt[n]{n(n + 1)(n + 2)\\cdots(2n - 1)}.$",
  "answer": "\\lim _ {n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac {1}{n} \\sqrt [ n ]{n (n + 1) (n + 2) \\cdots (2 n - 1)} = e ^ {2 \\ln 2 - 1} = \\frac {4}{e}.",
  "ref_source": "textbook:puheping_math_contest_v2",
  "techniques": [
    "极限计算"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "s1",
        "text": "分析 这是无穷乘积问题，取对数化为无穷和，容易看出用定积分定义计算很方便."
      },
      {
        "id": "s2",
        "text": "令 $a_{n} = \\frac{1}{n}\\sqrt[n]{n(n + 1)(n + 2)\\cdots(2n - 1)} = \\sqrt[n]{\\left(\\frac{1}{n} + 1\\right)\\left(\\frac{2}{n} + 1\\right)\\cdots\\left(\\frac{n - 1}{n} + 1\\right)}$ 。则"
      },
      {
        "id": "s3",
        "text": "\\ln a _ {n} = \\frac {1}{n} \\sum_ {k = 1} ^ {n - 1} \\ln \\left(1 + \\frac {k}{n}\\right),"
      },
      {
        "id": "s4",
        "text": "\\lim _ {n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\ln a _ {n} = \\lim _ {n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac {1}{n} \\sum_ {k = 1} ^ {n - 1} \\ln \\left(1 + \\frac {k}{n}\\right) = \\int_ {0} ^ {1} \\ln (1 + x) d x = 2 \\ln 2 - 1."
      },
      {
        "id": "s5",
        "text": "故"
      },
      {
        "id": "s6",
        "text": "\\lim _ {n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac {1}{n} \\sqrt [ n ]{n (n + 1) (n + 2) \\cdots (2 n - 1)} = e ^ {2 \\ln 2 - 1} = \\frac {4}{e}."
      }
    ],
    "final_answer": "\\lim _ {n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac {1}{n} \\sqrt [ n ]{n (n + 1) (n + 2) \\cdots (2 n - 1)} = e ^ {2 \\ln 2 - 1} = \\frac {4}{e}.",
